>I've seen much talk about generating custom levels. How does one go
>about this? There doesn't seem to be any information on it in any
>of the documentation.

There are two programs - dgn_comp and lev_comp - that are used for level
creation. The latter compiles the levels from text files and the former
connects the levels together, making the dungeon.

Neither of these is bundled with the MS-DOS binaries distributions
(don't know about other binaries).

In the source distribution tree, the source for the programs is in
the util directory, the documentation in doc/*.1 (in UNIX man page/nroff
format) and the existing levels (serving as examples) in dat/*.lev. So
just compile the programs and start making levels!

